course: dictionary
lesson: 13315
title: Grinning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Grinning means smiling widely, often so widely that you can see your teeth. «Mia came out of the classroom, grinning.» Mia is pleased, and her face shows it.
explain: Look at the words around grinning to check its meaning. «Grinning from ear to ear» is a phrase for smiling as widely as you can. «Stop grinning!» tells you someone is smiling in a cheeky way, perhaps because they got away with something.
explain: Grinning can also be an adjective, a word that describes a noun. «The grinning boy waved from the bus.» Here grinning tells you what sort of boy he is: one with a big smile on his face.
fact: Grinning means smiling widely, often showing the teeth.
fact: Grinning is the -ing form of the verb grin: grin, grins, grinned, grinning.
fact: «Grinning from ear to ear» means smiling very widely.
fact: «Grinning like a Cheshire cat» means smiling in a sly, pleased way.
fact: A grin can show that someone is pleased, amused or cheeky.
exercise: «Sam kept grinning after he won the race.» What does grinning mean here? | Running very fast | Crying loudly after the race | *Smiling widely, pleased with his win | Sitting down quietly
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes the boy: «The grinning boy waved from the bus.» | bus | *grinning | waved | boy
exercise: «She sat at the back, grinning like a Cheshire cat.» What does this suggest about her? | She is angry and shouting | She is fast asleep | *She is pleased and a bit sly | She is very cold and shivering
test: Which phrase means smiling as widely as you can? | *Grinning from ear to ear | Hiding under the desk | Frowning at the teacher | Yawning all afternoon
test: «Stop grinning, Ben, you know you broke the vase.» What does this tell you about Ben? | He is very sad and crying | *He is smiling in a cheeky way | He is freezing cold | He is ill in bed
exam: «The grinning clown handed out balloons, and the children ran to him.» What does grinning mean here? | Hiding behind the tent | Falling over in the grass | *Smiling widely, showing his teeth | Shouting at the children
